# Grid and layout

The engine, painting, hairlines, and lattice alignment live in
`design-system/grid/engine.css`. These laws govern on top of them.

## The band system

Five anchors where a design exists and renders exact; four structural gates
at the bands' geometric midpoints, gated by **container queries** on
`.site-root` — never media queries.

| band | gate (`@container min-width`) | anchor | tick `--t` |
|---|---|---|---|
| base | — | 384 | 32px |
| `rs` | 470 | 576 | 48px |
| `rt` | 665 | 768 | 64px |
| `rd1` | 860 | 960 | 80px |
| `rd2` | 1130 | 1344 | 112px |

- The tick is the page container's width ÷ 12, capped at 112px. Base CSS is
  the 384 design (mobile-first); each gate overrides upward.
- **Nearest-anchor rendering.** Every width renders the nearest anchor's
  design: stretched below its anchor, compressed above the gate. In a
  compressed slice the weights collapse to a pure zoom of that anchor, so wrap
  counts and designed clearances hold by construction.
- Above 1344 the tick caps, the weights pin at 0/1, and the 1344 design
  renders byte-exact at every wider width. The page box (12t) centers on a
  whole-pixel offset (`--page-x`); the freed gutters paint the side fields
  (`.gf-*`, deterministic server-side hash, never animated). Fixed chrome
  carries `--page-x`.
- Three-anchor pages may be designed at 384 · 768 · 1344 only. `rs` renders
  the 384 design on its tick; `rd1` derives from the 1344 design unless the
  section rules otherwise. A frame drawn later supersedes the derivation.
- JavaScript that needs the band measures the container (ResizeObserver) or
  reads computed style — never `matchMedia`.
- Every section is verified at all five anchors and one width per structural
  slice, scrollbar forced on.

## The four units

Every dimension belongs to exactly one unit. Classifying it is the first
decision.

1. **Ticks** — structure: column positions, section heights, exposure regions,
   component footprints. Written in `--t`; fluid by construction.
2. **Weights** — text columns: wrap-pinning widths and text-block heights in
   flow margins interpolate `calc(var(--wA)*V0 + var(--wB)*V1)` between the
   band's anchors.
3. **Em at anchor ratios** — line-internal spacing: inline gaps, chip paddings
   ride the type.
4. **Material** — fixed px per band: buttons, icons, marks, control inners.
   Primitives are material (fixed px per size variant, never band-aware);
   sections choose the size variant per band and own each instance's width.

A px value that secretly encodes ticks, weights, or type is a defect: it breaks
rag, fit, or clearance in the compressed slices. Constants that reference `--t`
or the weights are declared on `.page`, never `:root`.

## The grid and type laws

- **Hold-then-switch.** Type interpolates between a band's two anchors only
  when both carry the same structure. At a structural switch, type holds its
  last designed value across the band and switches with the structure at the
  gate.
- **Size and line-height interpolate; weight and tracking are band
  constants**, restated per band.
- **Band constants ride the weights.** A designed value constant across a band
  is `calc((var(--wA) + var(--wB)) * V)`, never `Vpx`, so it zooms with the
  tick in the compressed slices. Fixed px broke wraps and rail clearance the
  day sections met the compressed slices.
- **Line-inclusive content boxes.** A bordered box whose edge lies on exposed
  lattice is sized `k·t + 1px`, so its border lands on the line's pixel. A box
  sized `k·t` exactly doubles the hairline.
- **The tick wins.** A whole-tick box height governs over its declared padding
  sum; slack compresses padding or sits as clear space.
- **Content clears the lattice.** Flowed content never touches a tick line or
  another block and keeps at least half a tick of vertical clearance from the
  next section or a bottom-anchored block. When new content overruns a
  fixed-frame template (the case-study pages), grow the frame by whole ticks
  (per-study `extraTicks` in the data module) so the next block starts on the
  next tick. Copy never silently compresses a gap. **The painted lattice rides
  the growth**: cells drawn against content (widenings beside stat rows, tail
  rails, their ornaments) shift with the frame; the leading rail extends. A
  cell left on its drawn row while content moves is a defect.
- **Derived states.** When design supplies one archetype state, siblings
  derive as the smallest whole-tick height that fits their content at the
  band's internals; the derivation is written in a comment at the value.
- **Choreographies settle.** A load choreography ends explicitly on the final
  beat's `animationend`; band-gated variants re-entering the tree have nothing
  to replay.
- **Proportional primitives.** A primitive may be declared proportional (the
  pricing button): every interior value is a designed-px-over-anchor-cell
  fraction, so a mount that passes the page tick scales the control with the
  grid. The tell in Figma: when a set's cells equal the anchor ticks
  (32/48/64/80/112), read those px as `1t`.
- **Overlay chrome** (the nav) never participates in a section's tick stack.
- **Audits at rest.** Mid-flight motion may be fractional-tick by design; the
  stack-sum, landmark, and exposed-cell clearance audits assert at rest in
  every state. A clearance failure is a collision first.
- **Rendered truth over metadata.** Every landmark is verified against
  rendered bounds, never Figma metadata `x`/`y`.

## Layout must scale — no fragile positioning

Absolute positioning is acceptable only for: media fills (`inset: 0;
object-fit: cover` in a grid-sized parent); the exposure vocabulary
(`--gx`/`--gy` ticks); overlay layers (nav chrome, modal backdrops, decorative
pseudo-elements, a menu anchored to its control); grid-coordinate frames whose
parent has an explicit tick height and whose edges are expressed in ticks or
anchor weights; a true escape from document flow (viewport-fixed controls).
Everything else is normal flow.

| Anti-pattern | Fix |
|---|---|
| Fixed px coordinates from Figma's ruler | ticks/weights, flex order + margin |
| Fixed px widths on text containers | weight-riding wrap boxes |
| Fixed px heights on sub-containers | whole-tick heights; "the tick wins" |
| `line-height: 0` as a spacing hack | flex column + gap |
| Magic gaps | tick or em expressions per the four units |
| Media queries for band switches | container queries at the gates |

Always: no fixed widths that overflow at 384; touch targets ≥ 44 × 44 px;
no hover-only interactions.
